coder › Implemented `toc(markdown)` in `src/toc.ts` and added tests in `src/toc.test.ts`, committed on branch `work/toc` as `7300083 "Implement toc(markdown) with tests"`.

What it does:
- Splits on `\r?\n`, toggles an `inCode` flag on lines matching `/^\s*```/` and skips headings inside fences.
- Matches `/^\s*(#{1,6}) (.*)$/` — 1–6 `#` followed by a literal space; level is the hash count, text is the rest trimmed.
- Slug: `text.toLowerCase().replace(/[^\p{L}\p{N}]+/gu, "-")` with leading/trailing dashes trimmed (Unicode letters/digits).
- Dedup via a `used` set plus per-base counter: first use keeps the base, repeats get `-2`, `-3`, …, skipping candidates already taken by another heading's slug.

Checks:
- `bun test`: 7 pass, 0 fail (levels/slugs, space-required rejection, whitespace trim, fenced-block ignoring, punctuation slugify, `-2`/`-3` dedup, case-insensitive dedup).
- No lint/typecheck configured in the project (`bun test` is the only script); ad-hoc `tsc --strict --module nodenext` on the two files only reports the expected `bun:test` resolution and `.js`-extension style errors under `nodenext`, not real code errors.

Decisions the plan didn't spell out: fence detection allows leading whitespace and any info string after the backticks; letter/digit classes are Unicode-aware (`\p{L}\p{N}`); an empty heading yields an empty slug.

